{"text": "December 22, 1982\n\nMr. Nelson Orna\nFabrica De Cigarillos El Progreso S.A.\nCasilla 17\nQuito, Ecuador\n\nDear Nelson: \u2018\nI have received the first 10 Kaba treated samples of the 1982 crop.\n\nThese samples are now being analyzed for concentration of methoprene. I\nwill inform you of these results as soon as they are available.\n\nWhat percentage Kabat treated 1980 and 1981 crops is being blended into\nyour current cigarette production? Please send me 2 cartons of the\ncigarettes which contain the Kabat treated tobacco, I want to have some of\nthe cigarettes analyzed for methoprene concentration. Also, send 2 cartons\nof cigarettes without the Kabat treated tobacco, if available.\n\nYour insect control report indicates that dafly fogging with VaponS 10\nkeeping the beetle infestation under control; however, treatment with\nVapona ie not necessary in Building E-1, Counts from traps 2 and 3 showno 88\ninsects trapped in this area since V1-30/82; therefore, fogging is not won\njustified. In the event that beetles are found in traps 2 or 3 in future\nmonitoring, Vapona fogging can then be resumed.\n\nTrap 7, Building E~3, is beginning to show an increase in insect\ncounts. I recommend that you fog this area daily for a period of 1 month;\nthen determine if the insect count has beenggufficiently lowered. If this\nPopulation continues to increase, Phostoxin\u00ae fumigation is the only\nalternative.\n\nPlease note in your next insect control report the trap number and\nstorage location of the 1982 Kabat treated tobacco, This information will\nbe of help to me in maintaining awareness of the Kabat progr\n\nThank you for your assistance.\n\nSincerely,\n\nH Co cctene\n\nFundamental R & D\n\nIpd\nxc: Mr. Larry M. McLawhorn\nMr. Mac Turner\nMr. Brian Smeeton\nDr. Herman Benezet\n\n\u20ac6\u20acD IIIS",
